- Story & Context: Local myth claims that during the Great Heatwave of 2003, the projectionists of Plaza Colón attempted to project a silent film made entirely of pressed cassava leaves spliced between gelatin strips. The taste of sweet, fermenting sugarcane rum hung heavy on the crowd's lips as the flickering light beamed onto the municipal water tower, triggering a spontaneous city-wide block party that lasted until the city's power grid surrendered. Though the physical theater burned out its generator that night, dancers swear the metallic sparkle of the glockenspiel and the rolling dembow never ceased echoing down the alleyways, immortalized by the final chant: "La luz no se apaga, solo echa raíces."
